  "recovery": [
    "Keep all changed IDs including deleted IDs; no pruning/TTL/cap",
    "Cold cursor or generation/schema/physical identity/version mismatch or cursor outside floor..head => reseed, not empty complete delta",
    "Missing/altered owned tables/index/triggers, clock invalidity, direct journal edits or schema drift => atomic reinstall new UUID generation",
    "Retain and advance a valid surviving clock on repair; a lost clock starts a new epoch at zero; compare revisions only within matching epochs",
    "Each read validates metadata/head and reads changed rows plus caller SQL under the same transaction",
    "Replacement during callback => error, discard result; later normal commits are handled by next cursor read (S5 owns publish validation)",
    "Unknown added unique constraints dirty feed on mutation, forcing reseed",
    "Destructive-DDL writer may need schema-cache read or reconnect after another connection repairs tracking",
    "Non-Unix feed reads fail closed until equivalent physical identity support; adapter installation still works"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Finite solves are not source-code, all-interleavings, SQL-equivalence, pagination, liveness or performance proofs",
    "Journal grows with historical distinct IDs; no silent prune",
    "No live profiler/restart/install; S5 subscription work and S6 hygiene remain downstream",
    "Ordinary SQL drift/corruption handled; hostile forging/restoring tracking and source metadata together is outside the trust boundary"
